<section id="dev-console" class="lp-anchor">
  <div class="lp-section-head">
    <span class="eyebrow lp-eyebrow">The dev console &middot; actionagent</span>
    <h2 class="no-top-margin">See your agents while you build</h2>
    <p class="paragraph m secondary">
      The dashboard is its own MIT gem: a Rails engine that mounts in your app. Add it, turn on local
      telemetry, and every generation appears at <code class="lp-inline-code">/activeagents</code> as a
      trace with a span waterfall, token counts and the agent release that produced it. It is the same
      engine the hosted platform runs, against your own database.
    </p>
  </div>

  <pre class="lp-code"><code><span class="p">$</span> bundle add actionagent
<span class="p">$</span> rails generate action_agent:install <span class="dim">&amp;&amp;</span> rails db:migrate

<span class="cm"># config/active_agent.yml</span>
<span class="y">telemetry</span>:
  <span class="y">enabled</span>: <span class="k">true</span>
  <span class="y">local_storage</span>: <span class="k">true</span>      <span class="cm"># open /activeagents</span></code></pre>

  <%= render "pages/sections/dashboard_bento" %>

  <p class="lp-family">
    <span>For a team or a fleet of apps,</span>
    <span>mount it in one shared app and point the others' telemetry at <code>&lt;mount&gt;/api/traces</code>, with your own authentication in front.</span>
    <a href="https://docs.activeagents.ai/framework/self-hosted-observability" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Self-hosted guide</a>
  </p>
</section>
